# known-ips.txt.example
#
# Optional list of known-bad IPs, pre-banned at install time (before fail2ban
# has a chance to catch them from live traffic).
#
# This is a SEED LIST format, not a maintained or currently-accurate blocklist.
# Attacker infrastructure churns constantly — treat it as a starting point and
# populate it from your OWN logs / threat intel.
#
# To use: copy this file to lib/known-ips.txt (without .example) and add the
# IPs relevant to your deployment. If lib/known-ips.txt doesn't exist, the
# install simply skips the pre-ban step.
#
# One IP per line. Lines starting with # are ignored. The addresses below are
# from the RFC 5737 / RFC 3849 documentation ranges and are placeholders only —
# replace them with real ones.

203.0.113.10
203.0.113.11
198.51.100.23
192.0.2.44
